--TEST--
Core\RateLimit::shed keys its own memory — two keys under one limit spend separate budgets and a third opens on a full one — `rule:core-classes/ratelimit-two-members` and ADR 0059 § 1
--FILE--
<?nvs
// ADR 0059 § 1's "a map in the calling core's own thread", asked as behaviour
// rather than as structure: `shed` holds one arrival time *per key*, so the
// `$key` argument is what separates one account's budget from another's. A
// limiter that kept a single arrival time — the shape a first implementation
// reaches for, and the shape a namespacing bug degenerates to — admits four of
// these eight and sheds the rest, while every individual line it prints is a
// sentence a correct limiter also prints.
//
// Four an hour for each of two keys, taken alternately. The burst defaults to
// the limit, so a key that owns its own budget admits all four at an instant.
int $admitted = 0;
int $stepped = 0;
int $paired = 0;

foreach (Core\Arr::range(1, 4) as int $n) {
    var $a = Core\RateLimit::shed("tenant:a", 4, 1h);
    var $b = Core\RateLimit::shed("tenant:b", 4, 1h);
    int $leftA = $a->remaining() as int;
    int $leftB = $b->remaining() as int;

    if ($a->allowed()) {
        $admitted = $admitted + 1;
    }
    if ($b->allowed()) {
        $admitted = $admitted + 1;
    }

    // Each key drains at its own rate through its own budget, so both report
    // the same figure at the same arrival — the count that a shared budget
    // fails at the first pair, where it would answer 3 and 2.
    if ($leftA == $leftB) {
        $paired = $paired + 1;
    }
    if ($leftA == 4 - $n) {
        $stepped = $stepped + 1;
    }
    if ($leftB == 4 - $n) {
        $stepped = $stepped + 1;
    }
}

echo "admitted ", $admitted, " of 8 across two keys, alternately", "\n";
echo "the two keys agreed on what was left ", $paired, " of 4", "\n";
echo "each key counted its own four down ", $stepped, " of 8", "\n";

// The other side of the same bound, per key: the fifth arrival on each is shed,
// which is what says the four above were one key's budget and not two halves of
// one shared one.
int $shedBoth = 0;
var $fifthA = Core\RateLimit::shed("tenant:a", 4, 1h);
var $fifthB = Core\RateLimit::shed("tenant:b", 4, 1h);
if (!$fifthA->allowed()) {
    $shedBoth = $shedBoth + 1;
}
if (!$fifthB->allowed()) {
    $shedBoth = $shedBoth + 1;
}
echo "each key spent its own budget and no more ", $shedBoth, " of 2", "\n";

// And a key neither of them touched still has its whole window: an absent entry
// is an unspent budget, not a shared one.
int $untouched = 0;
var $third = Core\RateLimit::shed("tenant:c", 4, 1h);
if ($third->allowed()) {
    $untouched = $untouched + 1;
}
if (($third->remaining() as int) == 3) {
    $untouched = $untouched + 1;
}
echo "a third key opened on a full budget ", $untouched, " of 2", "\n";
--EXPECT--
admitted 8 of 8 across two keys, alternately
the two keys agreed on what was left 4 of 4
each key counted its own four down 8 of 8
each key spent its own budget and no more 2 of 2
a third key opened on a full budget 2 of 2
